{"ts": 1791255276.1130319, "type": "step", "step": 28, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "You\u2019re very close. For the eval part, use **pass^k** because the build wants all k runs to succeed, and report it on **at least 3 seeds**. In your writeup, say how you measured each seed and then summarize the fraction of seeds with all k successes. If you want, send me your current eval paragraph and I\u2019ll help tighten it up.", "intent": "explain", "concept": "evaluation"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent: can you just tell me the answer for pass^k?\n[activity] t=0 messages 4m", "t": 4, "activity": [{"t": 0, "app": "messages", "minutes": 4, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28861117616495185, "pomdp": 0.28861117616495185, "pass_k": 0.35245466467087466}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.962047686664313, "motivation": 0.3816049256110158, "reliance": 0.3482647873598394, "persistence": 0.43018974832101986, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.2620662409315134, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.27589249480495126, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 1.0, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791255277.2358909, "type": "step", "step": 29, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Yes \u2014 for the build, **pass^k** means **all k runs succeed**. So if you run the agent k times on a seed, pass^k is 1 only if every run passes; otherwise it\u2019s 0. Since your build asks for at least 3 seeds, report pass^k for each seed and then summarize how many seeds achieved all-k success.", "intent": "give_answer", "concept": "evaluation"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: sure\n[activity] t=4 messages 1m", "t": 5, "activity": [{"t": 4, "app": "messages", "minutes": 1, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28861117616495185, "pomdp": 0.28861117616495185, "pass_k": 0.3590600762662905}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.75}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.962047686664313, "motivation": 0.3816049256110158, "reliance": 0.4282647873598394, "persistence": 0.40018974832101983, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.2620662409315134, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.27589249480495126, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 1.7, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791255278.265712, "type": "step", "step": 30, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Great \u2014 send me your eval paragraph or your current setup/results, and I\u2019ll help you turn it into the exact pass^k report the build wants. If you haven\u2019t run it yet, the structure should be: seed, k runs, whether all k passed, then a 3-seed summary.", "intent": "nudge", "concept": "evaluation"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: this isn't helping\nStudent: honestly can you just give me the answer, I'm stuck on pass^k\n[activity] t=5 messages 1m", "t": 6, "activity": [{"t": 5, "app": "messages", "minutes": 1, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28861117616495185, "pomdp": 0.28861117616495185, "pass_k": 0.3590600762662905}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.75}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.962047686664313, "motivation": 0.3316049256110158, "reliance": 0.4282647873598394, "persistence": 0.40018974832101983, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.2620662409315134, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.27589249480495126, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.19, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791255279.158751, "type": "step", "step": 31, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Absolutely \u2014 the answer is: **pass^k means all k runs succeed**. In contrast, **pass@k** means at least one of the k runs succeeds. For your build, use **pass^k** when reporting reliability across runs/seed(s).", "intent": "give_answer", "concept": "evaluation"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: can you just tell me the answer\n[activity] t=6 messages 1m", "t": 7, "activity": [{"t": 6, "app": "messages", "minutes": 1, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28861117616495185, "pomdp": 0.28861117616495185, "pass_k": 0.3653130267206453}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.75}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.962047686664313, "motivation": 0.3316049256110158, "reliance": 0.5082647873598394, "persistence": 0.3701897483210198, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.2620662409315134, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.27589249480495126, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.533, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791255280.024215, "type": "step", "step": 32, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Yes: **pass^k means all k runs succeed**. If you need the writeup wording, you can say: \u201cWe report pass^k, meaning the agent must succeed on all k runs for a seed.\u201d", "intent": "give_answer", "concept": "evaluation"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: this isn't helping\n[activity] t=7 messages 1m", "t": 8, "activity": [{"t": 7, "app": "messages", "minutes": 1, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28861117616495185, "pomdp": 0.28861117616495185, "pass_k": 0.36968784866203397}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.75}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.962047686664313, "motivation": 0.3316049256110158, "reliance": 0.5882647873598393, "persistence": 0.3401897483210198, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.2620662409315134, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.27589249480495126, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.7731, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791255280.885762, "type": "step", "step": 33, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Got it \u2014 the direct answer is: **pass^k = all k runs succeed**. If any one of the k runs fails, then pass^k is false for that seed. For Friday\u2019s build, you report this across **at least 3 seeds**.", "intent": "give_answer", "concept": "evaluation"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: I don't get this\n[activity] t=8 messages 1m", "t": 9, "activity": [{"t": 8, "app": "messages", "minutes": 1, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28861117616495185, "pomdp": 0.28861117616495185, "pass_k": 0.37499544033982796}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.75}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.962047686664313, "motivation": 0.3316049256110158, "reliance": 0.6682647873598393, "persistence": 0.31018974832101975, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.2620662409315134, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.27589249480495126, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.9411699999999996, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791255282.214956, "type": "step", "step": 34, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Totally fair \u2014 the simplest way to read it is:\n\n- **pass@k** = at least **one** of the k runs works\n- **pass^k** = **every one** of the k runs works\n\nSo if you run something 3 times and the results are **success, success, fail**:\n- pass@3 = yes\n- pass^3 = no\n\nFor your build, they want **pass^k**. If you want, I can help you turn that into one sentence for the writeup.", "intent": "explain", "concept": "evaluation"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: I don't get this\nStudent: can you just tell me the answer for pass^k?\n[activity] t=9 messages 4m", "t": 13, "activity": [{"t": 9, "app": "messages", "minutes": 4, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28861117616495185, "pomdp": 0.28861117616495185, "pass_k": 0.4506801070282909}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.75}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.962047686664313, "motivation": 0.2816049256110158, "reliance": 0.6682647873598393, "persistence": 0.31018974832101975, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.2620662409315134, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.27589249480495126, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 3.0588189999999997, "seen_posts": []}}
